**Total "54-slots"** across all positions: 35 + 2 + 35 + 36 = 108. Each of the 36 integers needs exactly 3 slots of 54 (since 3·54 + 35·53 = 162 + 1855 = 2017), requiring 36·3 = 108 slots. ✓

**Slot assignment:** Give all 36 integers one slot at position 38 (36 slots). Give 35 integers a slot at position 37 (35 slots). The remaining integer gets 2 slots at position 36 (which has 2 slots). The 35 integers with 2 slots each get 1 more from positions 1–35 (35 slots). This accounts for all 108 slots, 3 per integer. ✓

**Verification of column sums:** Each column sums to 2017 by construction. **Verification of row sums:** Rows 37, 38 sum to 2017 ✓; each row i ≤ 36 sums to 3·54 + 35·53 = 2017 ✓.

By the integer Birkhoff–von Neumann theorem, M decomposes into 2017 permutation matrices, giving 2017 valid rankings. In this construction, a_k = 38 for k = 1,…,36 and a_k = 37 for k = 37,38, yielding sum = 1442.

**Conclusion.** The maximum possible value is **1442**.

